@startuml
title Stage 0.5 - High-Level Component Overview (No RTSP ingest)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Executable" {
  [main] as Main
}

package "Nodes (1 thread per node)" {
  [DecodeNode] as Decode
  [DummyDetectionNode] as Detect
  [OutputNode] as Output
}

package "Queues (pointer only)" {
  [BoundedPointerQueue<FrameMetadata*>] as Q1
  [BoundedPointerQueue<FrameMetadata*>] as Q2
}

package "Stores (single owner; nodes hold handles/pointers only)" {
  [FrameMetadataStore] as FrameStore
  [FrameBufferStore] as BufferStore
  [ObjectMetadataStore] as ObjectStore
}

package "Runtime / Observability" {
  [ChannelState] as ChannelState
  [ChannelRuntimeMetaStore\n(mutex backend; read=find-only; write=create)] as MetaStore
  [NodeRuntimeStateStore\n(node_instance_id -> counters/state)] as NodeStateStore
  [Logger] as Logger
}

Main --> Decode : construct & start thread\n(assign node_instance_id)
Main --> Detect : construct & start thread\n(assign node_instance_id)
Main --> Output : construct & start thread\n(assign node_instance_id)

Decode --> Q1 : push FrameMetadata*
Detect --> Q1 : pop FrameMetadata*
Detect --> Q2 : push FrameMetadata*
Output --> Q2 : pop FrameMetadata*

Decode --> FrameStore : acquire/release
Decode --> BufferStore : acquire/fill/release via handle
Detect --> ObjectStore : acquire object meta\nattach handles into FrameMetadata
Output --> ObjectStore : release objects\n(release chain start)
Output --> BufferStore : release buffers
Output --> FrameStore : release frame metadata\n(release chain end)

Decode --> ChannelState : decoded/dropped counter
Detect --> NodeStateStore : in/out/drop counters
Output --> NodeStateStore : in/out counters\n(+ future: error/drop)
Detect --> MetaStore : write(ChannelIdentifier)
Output --> MetaStore : read(ChannelIdentifier)\nTTL presence check
Logger <-- Decode
Logger <-- Detect
Logger <-- Output

note right of Decode
Stage 0.5: DecodeNode generates frames synthetically.
Connecting real RTSP input is considered Stage 1.
end note

@enduml
